# LinkedIn Share Link Issue - January 2026

## Summary
LinkedIn is manipulating official share links in posts, converting HTTPS to HTTP, displaying incorrect canonical URLs, and redirecting user traffic to business/LLC accounts instead of the intended personal profile.

## Observed Behavior

1. **HTTP Downgrade**: Official share link is being displayed as HTTP instead of HTTPS
   - Expected: `https://linkedin.com/in/[profile]`
   - Actual: `http://linkedin.com/in/canonical`

2. **Traffic Redirected to Business Entity**: The link preview shows a completely different BUSINESS profile
   - Expected: Nicholas Angell's personal profile
   - Actual: "C L. - Artist - Do Possible LLC" (a business/LLC)
   - This means personal share links are being hijacked to redirect traffic to business accounts

3. **Dynamic Link Manipulation**: The link changes in real-time after posting
   - Initially shows: `http://linkedin.com/in/canonical`
   - Later changes to: `https://lnkd.in/ejBVZZfb`

## Evidence
Screenshots captured at 2:56 PM showing:
- Post composition with incorrect canonical URL
- Saved post displaying HTTP link
- Link preview showing wrong user profile

